From c63b04d00d8df036f11cba37a004dc8c43b57faf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 22:48:40 +0000
Subject: input: usb_kbd_hid: keep polling after a transient poll error

usb_kbd_poll() returned early on any poll error other than -EAGAIN.
This skipped the poller_call_async() reschedule at exit, so the
keyboard poller died permanently after a single non-EAGAIN error.

A poller should never die on a recoverable error: a control endpoint
stall clears on the next SETUP packet, and the poller only needs to
keep running for that recovery to happen.

Observed on hardware: kbd-hid poll failed with -EPIPE right after
reaching the barebox prompt, then stopped responding for the rest of
boot. At this point in the driver's fallback logic, an -EAGAIN from
the interrupt-endpoint probe test routes to the control-endpoint
GET_REPORT path (usb_kbd_cnt_poll), and the keyboard firmware's
GET_REPORT handler is an unimplemented stub that always STALLs. This
patch alone does not make the control-endpoint path work; that
request keeps failing on every poll regardless. It only stops the
poller from dying, which matters because the real fix (routing around
this fallback and using interrupt-endpoint polling instead) depends
on the poller still being alive to retry.

Fix: goto exit instead of returning, so the poller reschedules
itself like the -EAGAIN case already does.

Signed-off-by: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
---
 drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c b/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
index 5b41be4dc8..5e4fa19341 100644
--- a/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
+++ b/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
@@ -108,7 +108,7 @@ static void usb_kbd_poll(void *arg)
 		/* exit with noreturn */
 		dev_err(&usbdev->dev,
 			"usb_submit_int_msg() failed. Keyboard disconnect?\n");
-		return;
+		goto exit;
 	}
 
 	if (!memcmp(data->old, data->new, USB_KBD_BOOT_REPORT_SIZE))
